BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Link Between Lifestyle and Cellular Aging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T200000
DTSTAMP:20260913T061709Z
UID:272db2aceab4119d@gid-seminars.wnprc.wisc.edu
CATEGORIES:Class/Seminar
DESCRIPTION:Everyone wants to feel healthy and vibrant. This is true no ma
 tter what decade of life you are in.   The good news is that you can take 
 steps now to improve the way you age at a cellular level. Cellular aging i
 s associated with your biological age\, which can be years younger or olde
 r than your chronological age\, as measured by your birth date.\n\nIn this
  noontime webinar\, you will learn the latest scientific research about th
 ree aging and chronic disease biomarkers: systemic inflammation\, oxidativ
 e stress\, and telomere length. Through practical insights and examples\, 
 you will discover how lifestyle factors like diet\, movement\, sleep\, str
 ess management\, and attitudes about aging can slow the cellular aging pro
 cess. Walk away with 1-2 actions you can start right away to improve the w
 ay you age moving forward\, no matter how old you are today.\n\nThis class
  will be recorded and a one-week link to the recording will be shared with
  all registered participants. \n\nThis class qualifies for double points a
 s part of our August promotion. To receive 4\,000 points\, attend at least
  80% of the live session or watch the entire recording within one week.\n
 \nRequest disability accommodations and access info.\n\n\n\nClass details 
 are subject to change.\n\nEvent URL: https://events.stanford.edu/event/the
 -link-between-lifestyle-and-cellular-aging-7478\n\nSource: stanford_virtua
 l
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-link-between-lifestyle-and-cellu
 lar-aging-7478
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: The Link Between Lifestyle and Cellular Aging
TRIGGER:-PT1H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
